## 1. Overview

This is a program written in C that verifies the validity of VLAN and port configurations on network devices.
We have implemented unit tests using Unity (ThrowTheSwitch) to perform boundary value analysis, edge-case testing, and code coverage measurement.

## 2. Development Environment

| Item | Details |
|---|---|
| Programming Language | C |
| C Standard | C11 |
| Compiler | GCC 16.2.0 |
| Testing Framework | Unity |
| Development Environment | MSYS2 UCRT64 |
| Code Coverage Measurement | gcov |

Unity commit: 54f864c

## 3. Implemented Features

### VLAN ID Validation
- Valid VLAN ID range: 1â€?4094
- Validation of multiple VLAN IDs using an array
- Referencing array elements using pointers
- NULL pointer check

### VLAN ID List Validation
- Management of VLAN IDs and the number of elements using a structure
- Stores up to 16 VLAN IDs
- Array bounds check
- Duplicate VLAN ID detection

### Port Configuration Validation
- Managing port modes using enums
- ACCESS mode: Specify one VLAN ID
- TRUNK mode: Specify 1â€?16 VLAN IDs
- Rejecting undefined port modes

*The port configuration rules are learning specifications defined for this project.

## 4. Test Design

We use Unity to automatically run unit tests.

Main Test Criteria:
- Normal and abnormal cases
- Boundary Value Analysis
- Array and pointer verification
- NULL pointer verification
- Structure and enum verification
- Array capacity limits and overflows
- ACCESS / TRUNK conditional branching

